// [user 2026-08-10] 633 cache lines REMOVED - deathvox (484), flvo (135), gurgle (13) and headshot
// (1) are now declared with `aliascache` in ubersound/, which precaches them inside CG_RegisterSounds
// during CA_LOADING (behind the loading screen) at ZERO configstrings and zero network traffic.
// Caching them HERE instead went through the server: script `cache` -> gi.soundindex() -> a CS_SOUNDS
// configstring -> the client registering it in CG_ConfigStringModified. That cost two things:
//   1. it burned 633 of MAX_SOUNDS (1600) server sound-index slots - almost certainly why that limit
//      kept being raised 512 -> 1024 -> 1280 -> 1600;
//   2. batched 25 files/frame, the later batches landed AFTER CS_PRIMED -> CS_ACTIVE, so the client
//      loaded them MID-GAMEPLAY - measured as 436 S_LoadSound calls in ~2 seconds right after spawn.
// Net memory cost of the move: zero. The same bytes were already resident; they now load earlier and
// in a better place. VERIFY with: grep S_LoadSound in qconsole.log - the engine prints
// "**************S_LoadSound: <path>" for every load OUTSIDE CA_LOADING (snd_mem_new.cpp:459-461),
// so that count should fall toward zero. Client ceiling is MAX_SFX 4096 (snd_local_new.h:181), a hard
// Com_Error - this fork exposes the live count as cvar s_sfxCount.
// !! If _research/gen_sndcache.py is ever re-run it will re-add these lines. It has been updated to
// skip the four aliascache-owned directories; check that before regenerating.
// HZM coop - voice-pool precache (bug-1141 lag spikes). GENERATED by gen_sndcache.py -
// do not hand-edit. The engine loads pool wavs lazily at FIRST PLAY (a synchronous
// disk read + decode mid-combat = hitch on kills/chatter). Cache the pools during the
// map's early frames instead, 25 files per frame.
